<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santo Domingo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Santo Domingo, on the south coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a>, was founded by the Spanish in the 1490s and is the oldest continuously inhabited European city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>. It was the seat of the first royal audiencia in the New World and the capital of the Spanish colony. Independence was proclaimed there in 1821 and again in 1844, and it is the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santo-domingo.jpg" alt="Santo Domingo" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jose Juan C · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SantoDomingoedit.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Juan Rodriguez, born in <b>Santo Domingo</b> of Portuguese and African descent, wintered on Manhattan in 1613–1614 trading for the Dutch, the first recorded non-Native inhabitant of the future New York City.</blockquote><a href="/empire/new-netherland">New Netherland · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Dessalines, Emperor Jacques I, had 3,000 to 5,000 remaining whites killed and was assassinated in 1806; Henri Christophe's northern kingdom and Alexandre Pétion's southern republic were reunited by Jean-Pierre Boyer in 1820, who conquered <b>Santo Domingo</b> in 1822.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-haiti">Republic of Haiti · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In February 1822 he occupied <b>Santo Domingo</b>, which had just declared independence from Spain, bringing the whole of Hispaniola under the republic and abolishing slavery there.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-haiti-1806-1849">Republic of Haiti (1806-1849) · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Cotubanamá was captured and hanged in <b>Santo Domingo</b>, ending the last independent chiefdom of Hispaniola.</blockquote><a href="/state/cacicazgo-of-higuey">Cacicazgo of Higüey</a></li><li><blockquote>Columbus founded La Isabela on the north coast of Hispaniola in 1493, and <b>Santo Domingo</b> was established on the south coast in 1496-98.</blockquote><a href="/state/captaincy-general-of-santo-domingo">Captaincy General of Santo Domingo</a></li><li><blockquote>An English expedition under William Penn and Robert Venables, part of Oliver Cromwell's Western Design, failed against <b>Santo Domingo</b> and seized lightly defended Spanish Jamaica in 1655.</blockquote><a href="/state/colony-of-jamaica">Colony of Jamaica</a></li></ul></section>
